WEBVTT

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:07.050
here. At other times, Chief Ironside has employed the services of, variously, a very small boy named

00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:12.060
Bobby, a police dog named Mike, and a minor bird named McCawber.

00:02:08.540 --> 00:02:13.840
To many people, the policeman appears in the role of adversary, both in its literal and legal meaning.

00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:20.310
This is not true. It is not the objective of the police to prosecute any citizen.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:27.120
It is our objective to obtain evidence of a crime and to compile such evidence in a manner directed by...

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:29.960
Excuse me, sir. This is urgent.

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:33.460
Thank you. Excuse me.

00:02:33.580 --> 00:02:43.340
We have to get these people out of here.

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:50.210
Ladies and gentlemen, due to unforeseen circumstances,

00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:51.890
I shall have to cut short my remarks.

00:02:51.890 --> 00:02:52.970
I trust you will excuse us.

00:02:56.610 --> 00:02:58.370
Please clear the building immediately, please.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:01.450
Immediately. Thank you.

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:04.400
We'll let you know in just a few minutes.

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:19.050
Get on the phone. Military Bomb Disposal Squad and tell them to get here as soon as possible.

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:20.000
We have a bomb.

00:03:20.910 --> 00:03:21.890
Ready to blow any time.

00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:29.750
It'll be here, it could be there.

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:38.740
The Big Bang could be anywhere, but when the clock tower sounds its bell, it could be your summons to dwell in hell.

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:22.540
Inside the main hall, they're running a circuit now.

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:25.380
Okay, side it, let's move it.

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:28.280
I don't have any trouble with these nuts.

00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:31.540
I wonder about you, Sergeant.

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:33.420
Didn't I tell you to check these suits?

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:34.940
How long does it take you to carry out an order?

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:36.140
Sorry, Mr. Simpson.

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:37.100
I won't have any answer.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.150
That's not the answer, Sergeant.

00:04:39.640 --> 00:04:41.220
I'm talking with some of you old sweats.

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:44.610
I think you don't think discipline applies to you.

00:04:45.770 --> 00:04:46.970
Discipline, Sergeant Brennan.

00:04:47.290 --> 00:04:50.050
Military discipline is that state of training and obedience

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:54.750
that makes for immediate carrying out of all orders of all lawful superiors.

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:55.310
Yes, sir.

00:04:56.210 --> 00:04:57.450
Very good, Sergeant.

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:01.140
All right, let's go.

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:02.080
Chief?

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:23.780
No answer.

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:25.240
Keep trying.

00:05:25.650 --> 00:05:26.010
All right.

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:31.080
Frank, Artie.

00:05:32.570 --> 00:05:33.430
What have we got, Sergeant?

00:05:33.530 --> 00:05:34.070
We don't know yet.

00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:36.810
If we don't turn it up in eight more minutes, we'll pull out.

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:40.960
What are you doing here?

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:43.260
Sir, I'm Neil Morgan, editor of the campus crowd.

00:05:43.260 --> 00:05:43.680
Get out of here.

00:05:43.880 --> 00:05:44.580
Just a minute.

00:05:44.840 --> 00:05:46.200
No time for arguments. Move.

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:47.660
I have a right to be here.

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:49.060
All right, get out or I'll run you in.

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:50.360
Come on, Neil, let's go.

00:06:02.620 --> 00:06:09.300
Over here, the drill.

00:06:12.750 --> 00:06:13.090
It's blanket.

00:06:13.620 --> 00:06:14.600
Okay, it's all yours.

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:15.360
Let's clear the area.

00:06:30.250 --> 00:06:30.690
You

00:07:09.404 --> 00:07:09.784
I don't know.

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:43.100
Sorry you missed all the fun.

00:07:43.360 --> 00:07:45.680
Yeah, there aren't many phone booths on that trial screen.

00:07:46.170 --> 00:07:48.480
Hey, this one calls it a student prank.

00:07:48.990 --> 00:07:49.930
Yeah, some prank.

00:07:50.890 --> 00:07:53.790
Don't they realize that prank tied up a number of police

00:07:53.790 --> 00:07:56.130
as well as scaring the daylights out of a lot of people?

00:07:56.310 --> 00:07:57.790
Chief, you gotta admit it's pretty funny.

00:07:57.930 --> 00:07:59.350
Two guys covered with talcum.

00:07:59.550 --> 00:07:59.970
Oh, ho.

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:05.480
Neil Morgan edits the school paper.

00:08:06.570 --> 00:08:06.970
Good morning.

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:09.130
Good morning, Mr. Morgan.

00:08:09.530 --> 00:08:10.940
Do you have an appointment?

00:08:11.510 --> 00:08:12.930
Sir, this is a public office.

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:15.300
As a member of the press, I am entitled to...

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:18.220
You're entitled to observe common rules of courtesy.

00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:21.960
When I'm ready to issue a statement, I'll see to it that you're informed.

00:08:22.040 --> 00:08:22.440
Good day.

00:08:22.680 --> 00:08:23.560
Now, just a minute, sir.

00:08:24.750 --> 00:08:25.470
I'm here to help.

00:08:26.300 --> 00:08:26.640
How?

00:08:27.550 --> 00:08:29.970
My assistant, Miss Henderson, and I have been up half the night as I...

00:08:30.420 --> 00:08:32.040
Good morning.

00:08:33.030 --> 00:08:34.150
Is that your data?

00:08:34.470 --> 00:08:34.950
Yes, sir.

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:41.030
I take it you don't consider last night's incident to be funny?

00:08:42.520 --> 00:08:43.680
Anything but funny, sir.

00:08:44.340 --> 00:08:46.240
I think it was more of a warning than anything else.

00:08:46.380 --> 00:08:47.140
What kind of warning?

00:08:47.830 --> 00:08:50.270
That it would be just as easy to plant a real bomb as a dummy.

00:08:51.180 --> 00:08:54.400
Now, why would anyone want to plant a bomb on the campus?

00:08:55.820 --> 00:08:57.820
Everybody knows what's been going on at school, sir.

00:08:58.920 --> 00:08:59.980
Well, a military...

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:03.300
left-wing minority has been trying to close down classes since the beginning of the term.

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:08.440
It's all there, sir. Clips from the Campus Daily as well as the local papers and wire service reports.

00:09:12.600 --> 00:09:19.590
I'm sorry. Chief Eve. Thank you very much, Mr. Morgan.

00:09:20.390 --> 00:09:26.320
Thank you. What have you got, Eve? Chief, Warren Officer Simpson here.

00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:28.530
Thank you.

00:09:30.480 --> 00:09:33.520
Good morning, Chief. We've got a real Rube Goldberg this time.

00:09:34.220 --> 00:09:35.680
Would you explain that, Mr. Simpson?

00:09:36.490 --> 00:09:40.510
It's a spring-activated gizmo connected to a timing device.

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:45.560
The timer activates the springs at the same time it sets off a penny torpedo.

00:09:46.170 --> 00:09:47.670
You know, the kind they used to sell for fireworks.

00:09:47.970 --> 00:09:49.690
What kind of workmanship went into it?

00:09:50.180 --> 00:09:52.400
Well, it's a pretty complicated device.

00:09:52.930 --> 00:09:55.750
I'd say somebody knew his bench mechanics to put it together so it would work.

00:09:56.720 --> 00:09:58.930
Thank you. Let me talk to Eve.

00:10:02.240 --> 00:10:02.600
Yes, Gene?

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:07.330
If the army's through with that device, bring it along.

00:10:08.020 --> 00:10:08.380
Yes, sir.

00:10:10.580 --> 00:10:12.940
I'm to take the device back to headquarters if you're through with it.

00:10:13.400 --> 00:10:14.120
What about it, Vernon?

00:10:17.210 --> 00:10:17.410
Sit.

00:10:17.730 --> 00:10:18.830
Going as far as I can go.

00:10:20.100 --> 00:10:21.120
Goodbye, and thank you.

00:10:21.630 --> 00:10:22.590
Drop in any time.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:31.400
You like anything.

00:10:34.120 --> 00:10:35.000
Is that a crack, Sergeant?

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:36.260
Just a passing remark.

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:42.550
How long have you been in the service, Sergeant?

00:10:43.490 --> 00:10:44.030
20 years.

00:10:44.840 --> 00:10:45.760
20 years?

00:10:46.290 --> 00:10:46.950
To make Sergeant?

00:10:49.460 --> 00:10:50.900
Not what I'd call an outstanding record.

00:10:51.700 --> 00:10:53.290
Oh, can't all be beavers.

00:10:54.140 --> 00:10:54.880
Come back here, Sergeant.

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:55.840
I'm not through talking to you.

00:10:58.500 --> 00:10:59.140
That's an order.

00:11:00.830 --> 00:11:02.490
Hey, Frank, what's wrong with you?

00:11:03.900 --> 00:11:04.600
What's wrong with me?

00:11:04.940 --> 00:11:05.980
Yeah, what's wrong with you?

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:07.460
You've been on my back for six months.

00:11:07.540 --> 00:11:08.240
I want to know why.

00:11:09.690 --> 00:11:10.310
Sit down, Arnie.

00:11:26.270 --> 00:11:27.810
You ever thought of transferring out of this unit?

00:11:27.950 --> 00:11:28.810
What are you talking about?

00:11:29.350 --> 00:11:29.970
I think the work's good.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:36.860
that's crazy i've been handling bombs for 18 years maybe you've been handling them too long

00:11:37.590 --> 00:11:45.180
everybody has a breaking point you're trying to tell me that i've lost my nerve no nothing like

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:51.650
that but you're reaching the point where your nerves gonna crack listen i've seen the signs

00:11:51.650 --> 00:11:56.350
before you miss details like not having the ties on that armor fixed

00:12:00.540 --> 00:12:01.000
Big deal.

00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:02.080
Little deal.

00:12:02.560 --> 00:12:03.700
Very small deal.

00:12:04.480 --> 00:12:05.200
But a symptom.

00:12:07.260 --> 00:12:09.140
And someday you'll miss another small deal.

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:13.240
Only that time the balloon will go up and take some other people along with it.

00:12:14.150 --> 00:12:15.470
You're afraid to work with me, aren't you?

00:12:16.190 --> 00:12:17.230
I didn't say that.

00:12:17.490 --> 00:12:18.930
You didn't say a lot of other things, too.

00:12:20.260 --> 00:12:21.040
What are you talking about?

00:12:21.320 --> 00:12:22.780
Like Darlene Hicks, for one.

00:12:24.660 --> 00:12:25.060
Darlene?

00:12:25.310 --> 00:12:26.590
Don't try to snow me, Frank.

00:12:26.790 --> 00:12:27.890
I know you're chasing her.

00:12:28.450 --> 00:12:29.570
Who needs to chase?

00:12:30.160 --> 00:12:31.940
Blow on her ear and she'll follow you anywhere.

00:12:35.060 --> 00:12:35.480
Easy.

00:12:37.040 --> 00:12:37.580
Down, boy.

00:12:38.930 --> 00:12:40.550
It's a year and a kick if you do.

00:12:41.700 --> 00:12:43.200
You pulling rank on me, Simpson?

00:12:45.640 --> 00:12:46.460
Okay, Sergeant.

00:12:46.740 --> 00:12:50.810
I tried to tell you for your own good to transfer out.

00:12:51.880 --> 00:12:54.480
You want to play it the hard way, you'll get it the hard way.

00:12:55.680 --> 00:12:56.880
That's all, Sergeant.

00:13:08.410 --> 00:13:10.270
Bomb disposal, Warrant Officer Simpson speaking.

00:13:12.500 --> 00:13:13.440
Yes, sir, we're rolling.

00:13:15.570 --> 00:13:17.210
Some duds on the artillery range.

00:13:17.680 --> 00:13:19.440
We've got to detonate them. Let's move it.

00:13:29.360 --> 00:13:29.880
Maybe Mr.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:30.960
Morgan has something.

00:13:31.680 --> 00:13:35.120
Seems a little rabid on the subject of student militants, wouldn't you say?

00:13:35.340 --> 00:13:36.320
He must have something.

00:13:36.380 --> 00:13:37.700
He wouldn't print names the way he does.

00:13:37.840 --> 00:13:38.780
There are libel laws.

00:13:39.820 --> 00:13:42.120
And you don't think it was a college prank?

00:13:42.670 --> 00:13:44.710
I can't see anybody taking the time and effort

00:13:44.710 --> 00:13:48.270
to put together a device with watchmaker precision just for last.

00:13:51.870 --> 00:13:52.870
Lab draw a blank, Chief.

00:13:52.990 --> 00:13:53.410
No fingerprints.

00:13:54.130 --> 00:13:55.290
What about the bomb container?

00:13:56.170 --> 00:13:57.330
Cardboard attaché case.

00:13:57.430 --> 00:13:58.590
They sell them at the five and dime.

00:13:59.570 --> 00:13:59.970
That leaves...

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:04.160
the note. Ironside, just a moment.

00:14:05.830 --> 00:14:07.070
Dean Morris at the college.

00:14:10.280 --> 00:14:15.670
Afternoon, Dean. We'll be right there.

00:14:16.840 --> 00:14:18.440
You've called bomb disposal unit.

00:14:18.700 --> 00:14:20.440
Tell Simpson to meet us at building C.

00:14:20.540 --> 00:14:21.120
Now let's go.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:46.760
Here it's I am. The students and faculty are out chiefs. This was delivered to my office 30 minutes ago.

00:14:49.580 --> 00:14:53.420
Hickory dickory dock, there's something in the clock. One, two, three, and up goes C.

00:14:54.600 --> 00:14:55.580
How is that note delivered?

00:14:56.340 --> 00:14:58.660
I had to have slipped through the mail slot in one of the outer offices.

00:14:59.070 --> 00:14:59.970
By the time one of the sec-

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:02.120
Secretaries noticed it. Whoever delivered it was long gone.

00:15:02.870 --> 00:15:06.540
Well, if the note means things are due to go up at three, it doesn't leave much time.

00:15:07.110 --> 00:15:07.430
Chief?

00:15:07.690 --> 00:15:07.870
Yeah?

00:15:08.340 --> 00:15:10.340
He says the bomb disposal unit's out in the field.

00:15:10.520 --> 00:15:12.820
They're trying to reach him by radio telephone, but so far no luck.

00:15:14.770 --> 00:15:15.770
We'll evacuate the building.

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:37.600
Neil, we have to evacuate.

00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:39.060
But this is news, Dean Morris.

00:15:39.200 --> 00:15:41.060
Neil, this place is liable to blow up at any moment.

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:43.200
All right, you, out of here.

00:15:44.180 --> 00:15:46.940
No luck. Searched every clock in the building.

00:15:47.120 --> 00:15:48.100
We better leave, Mark.

00:15:50.200 --> 00:15:52.500
It's a very dickory, Doc. Something's in the clock.

00:15:53.180 --> 00:15:53.740
You said something?

00:15:54.000 --> 00:15:54.620
Clock. Clock.

00:15:55.460 --> 00:15:56.080
Dr. Morris?

00:15:56.260 --> 00:15:56.540
Yes?

00:15:57.040 --> 00:15:59.100
Is there any particular clock in this building?

00:15:59.260 --> 00:15:59.980
Something that would be...

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:04.610
known as the clock, something everyone on campus would know about. What about Professor Spencer's

00:16:04.610 --> 00:16:09.340
water clock? Water clock? It's a sort of a campus joke, Chief. Spencer spent years perfecting it.

00:16:09.520 --> 00:16:24.010
Where is it? The third floor, Spencer's laboratory. Mark, move. I said get out of here,

00:16:24.090 --> 00:16:27.490
now that's an order. What are you going to do about it?

00:16:36.270 --> 00:16:37.450
Be a blasted fool.

00:16:37.550 --> 00:16:46.610
See, if this isn't funny, how does it work?

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:49.860
It's not supposed to tick, I can tell you that.

00:16:52.100 --> 00:16:53.100
Put some water in that sink.

00:16:55.180 --> 00:16:56.220
Now throw me that stool.

00:17:48.970 --> 00:17:49.930
It won't explode, will it?

00:17:50.700 --> 00:17:53.080
Not unless some chemical genius has been at work.

00:17:54.020 --> 00:17:55.120
That's household putty.

00:18:04.540 --> 00:18:09.620
Bomber struck again today, but the only damage suffered was to the nerves of the police and

00:18:09.620 --> 00:18:16.180
university officials. An explosive device, similar to the one found in University Hall last night,

00:18:16.700 --> 00:18:22.080
was discovered today in a university science building. Wow, what a gruesome sense of humor.

00:18:22.900 --> 00:18:27.060
Say that again. Who would do such rotten things? There are a lot of creeps around campus.

00:18:28.310 --> 00:18:29.770
The thing that bothers me is...

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:33.700
Sooner or later, whoever's playing these tricks may decide to plant a real bomb.

00:18:34.590 --> 00:18:37.450
For all practical purposes, this was a real bomb.

00:18:38.390 --> 00:18:38.850
What do you mean?

00:18:39.820 --> 00:18:43.210
Whoever rigged up that dummy used a fulminator mercury cap.

00:18:43.640 --> 00:18:44.680
That's what caused the explosion.

00:18:45.140 --> 00:18:45.500
Dangerous?

00:18:45.720 --> 00:18:47.480
No, sir. One of them can blow your hand off.

00:18:47.600 --> 00:18:50.390
Not this one. Whoever did it removed most of the charge.

00:18:50.590 --> 00:18:52.250
Wasn't any stronger than a cannon cracker.

00:18:52.510 --> 00:18:53.290
You didn't tell me that.

00:18:54.640 --> 00:18:55.300
You didn't ask me.

00:18:56.550 --> 00:18:57.970
From now on, you keep me informed.

00:18:59.630 --> 00:18:59.890
Yes.

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:01.260
So, Mr. Simpson, sir.

00:19:01.480 --> 00:19:06.560
Honey, would you say that the man who made this bomb was familiar with explosives?

00:19:06.880 --> 00:19:07.800
I bet he was.

00:19:08.590 --> 00:19:09.190
Excuse me, Chief.

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:11.000
I got a date.

00:19:11.500 --> 00:19:12.320
At ease, Sergeant.

00:19:13.470 --> 00:19:14.310
You had a date.

00:19:15.340 --> 00:19:16.440
You're pulling CQ tonight.

00:19:20.280 --> 00:19:21.060
Pulled it last night.

00:19:22.020 --> 00:19:24.400
And you've been getting pretty lippy so you can pull it again tonight.

00:19:26.700 --> 00:19:27.420
What are you waiting for?

00:19:28.440 --> 00:19:29.740
A card for the chaplain to punch?

00:19:31.470 --> 00:19:33.820
You can't do this to me. It's against regulations.

00:19:34.510 --> 00:19:37.840
R-H-I-P, Sergeant. Ask any officer.

00:19:38.870 --> 00:19:39.350
Good night, Chief.

00:19:42.620 --> 00:19:43.720
R-H-I-P?

00:19:45.250 --> 00:19:46.710
Rank has its privileges.

00:19:47.320 --> 00:19:49.180
Well, this kind of a thing could go too far.

00:19:50.920 --> 00:19:54.640
All right. Could you make some coffee, please, and then turn on the news?

00:19:55.820 --> 00:19:57.000
I wanted to look at the fights.

00:19:59.460 --> 00:19:59.680
News.

00:20:00.604 --> 00:20:01.564
R-H-I-P.

00:20:02.940 --> 00:20:03.700
Like I said.

00:20:04.700 --> 00:20:07.400
This kind of a thing can be pushed too far.

00:20:09.308 --> 00:20:09.668
Century.

00:20:10.780 --> 00:20:12.360
Now, these big letters are 24 point.

00:20:13.052 --> 00:20:14.352
Small ones are 18 point.

00:20:15.068 --> 00:20:16.628
Now, the real small ones are regal.

00:20:16.956 --> 00:20:17.556
Body type.

00:20:17.820 --> 00:20:18.760
About, uh...

00:20:19.068 --> 00:20:20.828
Oh, eight point on a nine point slot.

00:20:22.012 --> 00:20:22.852
Well, that's centuries.

00:20:23.388 --> 00:20:24.288
Real nice tight.

00:20:25.276 --> 00:20:26.776
Pity it ain't being used much anymore.

00:20:28.476 --> 00:20:29.976
Everybody's going for that moderate.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:32.450
and sans serif. Skinny stuff.

00:20:32.650 --> 00:20:35.370
It had no character to it.

00:20:35.920 --> 00:20:38.030
Doesn't anybody use Century? Oh, yeah.

00:20:38.070 --> 00:20:41.250
Job shops use it to print up

00:20:41.250 --> 00:20:42.850
old school papers,

00:20:42.950 --> 00:20:43.990
church publications.

00:20:45.000 --> 00:20:45.360
like that

00:21:10.140 --> 00:21:10.760
What can I do for you?

00:21:12.110 --> 00:21:12.970
I'm Eve Whitfield.

00:21:18.610 --> 00:21:19.480
That's nice.

00:21:19.680 --> 00:21:22.790
Dean Morris sent me over for a tryout.

00:21:22.970 --> 00:21:27.520
You're new here, aren't you?

